---
import Marketing from "../layouts/Marketing.astro";
---

<Marketing
  title="Download previews — Alkemyst"
  description="Preview availability, target platforms, and source-build guidance for Alkemyst."
>
  <section class="wrap page-intro">
    <p class="eyebrow">EARLY DEVELOPMENT</p>
    <h1>Download previews</h1>
    <p class="lead">Preview installers are not published yet.</p>
    <p>
      We are verifying native builds and the window, tray, tracking, and MCP lifecycle before
      distributing a preview. There is no stable release.
    </p>
    <a class="button secondary" href="https://github.com/ebursztein/alkemyst/releases">
      View GitHub Releases
    </a>
  </section>
  <section class="wrap platform-section" aria-labelledby="platforms-title">
    <h2 id="platforms-title">Target platforms</h2>
    <div class="platforms">
      <article>
        <p class="eyebrow">MACOS</p>
        <h3>Apple Silicon</h3>
        <p>macOS 13 or newer.</p>
        <p class="status">Installer pending</p>
      </article>
      <article>
        <p class="eyebrow">WINDOWS</p>
        <h3>64-bit Intel / AMD</h3>
        <p>Windows 11, x64.</p>
        <p class="status">Installer pending</p>
      </article>
    </div>
    <p>
      Check each release’s notes for the platforms actually verified. Linux and Intel Macs are not
      distribution targets for the initial preview.
    </p>
  </section>
  <section class="wrap page-section">
    <h2>Build a reviewed revision</h2>
    <p>
      Developers can build the app from source with the pinned Node, pnpm and Rust toolchains. Use a
      reviewed tag or pull-request head; unreleased code may not be on the main branch yet.
    </p>
    <a href="/docs/guides/development/">Source-build instructions →</a>
  </section>
  <section class="wrap page-section">
    <h2>When a preview becomes available</h2>
    <p>
      Installers and SHA-256 checksums will live on GitHub Releases. Early previews may be unsigned
      or ad-hoc signed, with their status stated in the release notes. Stable distribution requires
      trusted signing and macOS notarization.
    </p>
    <p>
      Follow the platform-specific instructions and checksum guidance attached to that exact
      release.
    </p>
    <a href="/docs/setup/">Setup and local-data guidance →</a>
  </section>
</Marketing>
